XY.CSV
  - Our xy.csv file has ';' as the delimiter, so if you want to run our code with another dataset (where the xy.csv file uses ',' as the delimiter), you will need to change this line:
    coordinates = pd.read_csv('xy.csv', delimiter=';')
    to
    coordinates = pd.read_csv('xy.csv', delimiter=',')
    Location of that line:
      - SINGLE: Line 245
      - MULTI: Line 232  


SINGLE-OBJECTIVE

  - RUN the Single-Optimization by running the following command: python .\SINGLE.py 
  - Input Parameters:
      - Number of cities (10, 30, 50)
      - Evaluate by cost or time (cost, time)
      - Choose transport (bus, train, plane, all)
      - Number of runs [1; 30]
      - Use heuritic (yes, no)
  - Prints in the terminal:
      - Mean of the best time/cost (depending on the evaluated parameter cost/time)
      - STD of the best tims/cost (also depending on the evaluated parameter cost/time)
      NOTE: If the number of the runs is 1 it will also print the STD ('nan'), and it will also give a warning based on that.
  - Plots: 
      - If the number of runs is 1, it will plot the best path for that run and the respective convergence curve.
      - If the number of runs is more than 1, it will plot only the convergence curve of the best run (but it will not plot the best path). 
      

MULTI-OBJECTIVE

  - RUN the Multi-Objective by running the following command: python .\MULTI.py
  - Input Parameters:
      - Number of cities (10, 30, 50)
      - Use heuritic (yes, no)
  - Prints in the terminal:
      - For the Min Cost it will print the cost and the time
      - For the Min Time it will print the cost and the time
  -Plots:
      - Pareto Curve
      - Best time for Min Cost
      - Best cost for Min Time
      - Pareto Curve with the Hypervolume Evolution Curve


ADDITIONAL INFORMATION (Additional files)

  DATASET
  - Command used for the creation of matrix_distances.csv: python .\calculate_dist.py
  - Command used for the creation of the 6 .csv files: python .\calculate_time_price.py
  - Command used to plot the selected cities in a planar map: python .\plot_map.py

  CONVERGENCE CURVES (SINGLE-OPTIMIZATION)
  - Our code only runs 30 times for one type of transport (or all), so it only produces 1 convergence curve at a time.
  - In order to generate only 2 plots (each one with 4 covergence curves) we used the last 4 lines of the code in SINGLE.py
    (which are commented), to save the convergence curve of all the transports in a .json file
  - With all the .json files generated, we ran the command "python .\plot_convergence_curves.py" and
    "python .\plot_heuristic_convergence_curves.py" for creating the plots with heuristic and no heuristic respectively.


